# SABOTAGE: an INERT operator breadcrumb trail — the reported "breadcrumbs don't work".
#
# Reverts `Samen.Web.Operator.AccountsLive`'s trail to the plain-string form every operator page
# used before `Crumbs.operator/0` existed. `Samen.UI.topbar/1` renders a plain string as INERT
# text and only a `{label, href}` tuple as a link, so the trail keeps its exact SHAPE and loses
# its live crumb: same crumbs, same labels, same order — only the click is gone. That is why the
# defect went unnoticed across a whole plane: nothing looks missing, the marker simply is not a
# link (and the plane declares no `/operator` index route, so there was nowhere to link it TO).
#
# The SWEEP leg of `operator_breadcrumbs_test.exs` is anchored on the LEADING crumb of every
# operator trail, so it must FLIP. The other legs stay green — the rendered Portfolio trail and
# the seam unit test are untouched by this patch — which is what attributes the flip to the CALL
# SITE rather than to the topbar's rendering.
#
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/operator_breadcrumbs_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: SWEEP: every operator trail LEADS with that live crumb (no inert operator trail)
diff --git a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/operator/accounts_live.ex b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/operator/accounts_live.ex
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/operator/accounts_live.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/operator/accounts_live.ex
@@ -146,7 +146,7 @@
           <.operator_sidebar mount={@samen_mount} active={:accounts} operator_role={assigns[:samen_operator_role]} />
         </:sidebar>
 
-        <.topbar title="Accounts" crumbs={[Crumbs.operator(), "Accounts"]}>
+        <.topbar title="Accounts" crumbs={["Operator plane", "Accounts"]}>
           <:actions>
             <.button :if={writable?(@samen_mount) and not @no_org} variant="primary" phx-click="new_account" id="new-account">
               <:icon>
